    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 asymmetric Fabry-Perot bandpass filter on Fused Silica substrate with Air incident medium. Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2 (20 finite layers total, alternating H/L starting with high-index Ta2O5). Initialize thicknesses using baseline values: [157.12, 333.24, 336.89, 284.43, 207.08, 310.49, 120.47, 211.41, 208.75, 286.48, 215.19, 336.73, 157.05, 322.90, 342.41, 254.64, 176.10, 258.47, 182.86, 375.56] nm. Apply optimization bounds of ±10 nm absolute offset from these initial values for each layer (e.g., layer 1: 147.12-167.12 nm, layer 2: 323.24-343.24 nm, etc.). Optimize for maximum transmittance at 1550 nm with strong suppression in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Wavelength range: 1400-1700 nm. Normal incidence (0 degrees). Unpolarized or average of TE/TM. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
